Changes since v3:
- For the opt-out model, dispatch_jump_p no longer asserts that
  TARGET_ASM_JUMP_TABLE_BASE is set.  With patch 3, the transformation
  runs on every port that does not opt out in patch 4, not only AArch64.
- find_dispatch_chain: stop at a fall-through edge when the jump at the
  end of its source, such as an asm goto, also targets the destination.
  In v3 the copy of that jump still named the original block, which can
  cause an ICE.
- New function fallthru_unified_with_branch_p does this check.  A new
  gcc_checking_assert in maybe_duplicate_dispatch applies it to each
  chain edge that moves to a copy.  New test switch-dispatch-run-8.c.
- find_dispatch_chain: count with duplication_unit and duplication_size
  of patch 1.  This changes only ports without a length attribute, where
  the v3 budget set no limit.  Some of them, such as ia64, now share
  tables (patch 3), so the limit now has an effect.
- New torture test switch-dispatch-run-5.c, to find ports that must opt
  out.  It sends each copy of its two switch dispatches to every case,
  hole, range end and type limit.  A trace checks the exact path.
- New torture tests switch-dispatch-run-6.c (-fpic) and
  switch-dispatch-run-7.c (-fno-pic) run switch-dispatch-run-5.c with
  large handlers, so that some copies are far from their table.
- New test gcc.dg/switch-dispatch-4.c: at -O2, switch-dispatch-run-5.c
  must have exactly two shared tables where the new effective target
  shared_jump_tables is true.  A port that does not share then FAILs.
- New effective target shared_jump_tables (lib/target-supports.exp,
  doc/sourcebuild.texi) lists where sharing is expected.  It is false
  for the opt-outs of patch 4 and where no jump table is emitted.
- New compile tests for the guards of patch 2: switch-dispatch-hwloop.c,
  switch-dispatch-placement.c, and bfin and xtensa switch-dispatch-1.c.
  The bfin and xtensa tests check that hw-doloop rejects the loop.
- tablejump_capability_plugin.cc: with TARGET_ASM_JUMP_TABLE_BASE unset,
  expect TARGET_CAN_SHARE_JUMP_TABLE_P to return true (patch 3 default).
  v3 expected false.  Call the saved base hook only if it is set.
- switch-dispatch-2.c and switch-dispatch-3.c require indirect_jumps.
  In v3 they were UNRESOLVED on nvptx.  switch-dispatch-2.c also sets
  max-goto-duplication-insns to 128 to test only the back-edge rule.
- switch-dispatch-run-1.c to switch-dispatch-run-4.c now use noipa.
- Documentation: doc/invoke.texi says that the transformation runs only
  with -fexpensive-optimizations and in functions optimized for speed.
  doc/params.texi says that max-goto-duplication-insns also limits it.
- common.opt.urls: add the entry for -fduplicate-switch-dispatch, which
  v3 did not have.
- The comments of find_dispatch_chain and maybe_duplicate_dispatch now
  say that MAX_SIZE limits the whole chain, not only BB.  Remove an
  empty-chain check in find_dispatch_chain that is never true.
- Commit message: describe the plain fall-through rule, the budget units
  and the new tests.  Say "the cfgrtl patch" in place of "the first
  patch", because patch 1 is now a different patch.

