+@opindex fduplicate-switch-dispatch
+@opindex fno-duplicate-switch-dispatch
+@item -fduplicate-switch-dispatch
+If supported by the target machine, give eligible predecessors of a switch at
+a loop head their own copy of the jump-table branch.  A bytecode interpreter
+written with such a @code{switch} otherwise sends every opcode transition
+through one indirect branch instruction.  This can make indirect target
+prediction less effective.  GCC already performs the same transformation for
+the computed gotos of an interpreter written with the labels-as-values
+extension.
+
+It trades size for speed, so the amount copied is bounded by
+@option{--param=max-goto-duplication-insns}.  The transformation runs only
+with @option{-fexpensive-optimizations} and only in functions that are
+optimized for speed.
+
 @opindex fif-conversion
